# Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, and every script here has a
# bash shebang. CRLF makes the kernel look for `bash\r`, and the frontmatter
# checks compare against a literal `---` that `---\r` never matches, so a
# Windows clone fails everywhere at once. Normalise on the way in and check
# out LF regardless of the setting.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
